README

March 2021:
	This folder contains all the code and data reported in our paper,
	
	"Novel Range Functions via Taylor Expansions and Recursive
		Lagrange Interpolation with Application to Real Root Isolation"
			by
		K.Hormann, L.Kania and C.Yap
	
	*A subfolder "data" contains of a suite of 16 real polynomials
			(chebyshev, hermite, wilkinson, sparse)
		of various degrees.  These are square-free polynomials.
	* We implemented the EVAL algorithm for isolating the
		real roots of a polynomial f(x) in a given interval [a,b].
	* There are 8 versions of EVAL, depending of the type of range
			function used to evaluate f(x) and f'(x).
		4 versions are based on Taylor forms
		4 versions are based on our new Recursive Lagrange forms
	* We have 3 experiments, producing 3 tables.
		Each table has 8 columns (for the 8 EVAL versions)
			and 16 rows (for the 16 polynomials).
		 Table1: shows the sizes of the subdivision trees
		 Table2: shows the average running time when the 
				arithmetic uses 1024-bit machine floating point 
		 Table3: shows the average running time when the
				arithmetic uses multi-precision rational numbers
		REMARK: we do not have two versions of Table1 because
		the tree sizes are little affected by the arithmetic used.
	* We have a Makefile with the targets:
			table1, table2, table3
		to automatically produce these tables.
